From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [vllm] fix: the sub-paged attention view for FlashInfer's
 fused K/V layout, and for HND

Local, from no pull request. LMCache pull request #4253 (https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/pull/4253) addresses
the same layout another way.

vLLM's FlashInfer backend registers each attention layer as a fused-K/V rank-4 tensor
(pages, num_kv_heads, kernel_block_size, 2 * head_size) and requires the HND layout. _SubpagedAttentionViewEdit only
matched rank-5 (pages, 2, ...) tensors, so under FlashInfer the edit never applied: the attention group stayed at the
kernel's page size while the scheduler's block is the recurrent-state page, LMCache classified it as a compressed
group, and store and retrieve moved a fraction of each block's KV, corrupting live KV on every load. The rank-4
branch re-views the tensor at the scheduler block size in the layout's own memory order
((blocks, 1, block_size, num_kv_heads * content) for HND, the NHD-strided equivalent otherwise); with one KV head per
rank the dims stay semantic. For the rank-5 layout the kernel block size is read from the layout's token dim (dim 3
under HND) instead of assuming NHD. Each group's kind, block size, page size, layout and registered tensor shape are
logged once at registration.
---
